+# gsDesign (development version)
+
+## Breaking changes
+
+- Analyses without a bound (zero incremental spending, or an analysis skipped
+  via `testUpper`, `testLower` or `testHarm`) are now represented by `-Inf`
+  (lower and harm bounds) and `Inf` (upper bound) instead of the finite
+  sentinel `-20`/`20`. This affects `gsDesign()`, `gsBound()`, `gsBound1()`,
+  `gsProbability()` and every function that reports these bounds. Infinite
+  bounds are accepted as input by `gsProbability()`, `gsBound1()`,
+  `gsDensity()` and `normalGrid()`. Numerically the change is negligible
+  (below 1e-30 unless the drift at a skipped analysis exceeds about 12
+  standard errors), but code that compared bounds against 20 must now use
+  `is.finite()`. `gsBoundCP()` returns `NA` for the conditional power at an
+  analysis without a bound.
+
+## Bug fixes
+
+- The Newton-Raphson boundary search in the C code no longer risks a `0/0`
+  step when a target crossing probability is zero and the density underflows
+  (for example with two analyses very close in information). Previously the
+  resulting `NaN` iterate was silently discarded because comparisons with
+  `NaN` end the iteration; the iteration cap (20) and the iterate clamp are
+  now named constants independent of the former `EXTREMEZ` sentinel.
+- `gsDensity()` no longer reads an undefined lower bound for one-sided
+  (`test.type = 1`) designs.
+
 # gsDesign 3.11.0 (August 2026)
 
 ## New features
